        "property_id": "PROP-0031",
        "title": "Does patricialize correctly create BranchNodes with 16 subnodes when keys have no shared prefix at the current level?",
        "severity": "High",
        "mindset": "Formal Verification Engineer",
        "is_boundary_check": false,
        "reachability": {
          "classification": "external-reachable",
          "entry_points": [
            "Transaction"
          ],
          "attacker_controlled": true,
          "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"
        },
        "test_procedure": "1. Create a trie with keys that diverge immediately at a given level.\n2. Trace patricialize and verify BranchNode is created.\n3. Verify BranchNode has exactly 16 subnodes (indices 0-15).\n4. Verify each key is placed in the correct branch based on its nibble at 'level'.\n5. Verify value field is populated only if a key terminates at this level.",
        "bug_class": "State Consistency",
        "risk_category": "Tampering",
